 "state": "predicted-static; import only after live capture confirms the key (validate_predicted.py confirm + gate on the AQ-03 Stage 3 capture)",
 "created_at_utc": "2026-11-13T21:40:12.569066+00:00",
 "method": "W7-STAGE3 index masters (copy of w7-stage2/tools/s2master.py; imports s3lib): one CLUT-free master per 4bpp page, rendered through any CLUT.\n\nMaster (8 px/texel = the 2048 export grid; CPU only, deterministic, no AI, nothing added):\n  categorical layer  top-3 (label, weight u8) per pixel: for every native index i the one-hot mask is upsampled\n                     texel-centred (bilinear), gaussian-smoothed (sigma_cat texels) and raised to power_cat, then\n                     normalised (w7-stage7 build_s7 / w4-world catsoft method). It carries the class (alpha) of ANY\n                     CLUT: class = class of the strongest visible label where visible weight >= 0.5, else 0, so every\n                     CLUT gets its own native class map with smooth contours.\n  continuous layer   t (float16, NaN elsewhere) inside regions whose drawn CLUTs are monotone luminance ramps over the\n                     indices used there (palette-cycling lights, smoke and flame ramps): normalised convolution of the\n                     native index over the texels that are visible in that region (bilinear texel-centred upsample,\n                     gaussian sigma_t texels); render = lerp(P[floor t], P[ceil t]) (index_pipeline convention), t\n                     clamped to the CLUT's visible run.\nRender(CLUT) -> RGBA at 8 px/texel; the native class is then forced at every native texel centre floor((i+0.5)*s)\n(one pixel each, w6/w7 rule) and every export is re-read and validated (0 mismatches required).\nRegions come from the Stage 2 draw records (work/draws-s2.json): every drawn uv rect of every key of the page whose CLUT\nwords are known (static export CLUT or CRC-validated recovered phase).",
 "builder_doc": "W7-STAGE3 builder: first Stage 3 art families on exact-static, single-writer pages of the frozen stages-v4 export.\n\n    python -I build_s3.py <family> [freeze]      family = walls | signage\n    -> staging/<name>/ (default) or frozen/<name>/ (freeze: immutable, refuses to overwrite)\n\nState of every key: predicted-static; import only after live capture confirms the key (validate_predicted.py confirm +\ngate on the AQ-03 Stage 3 capture).  No Stage 3 capture exists, so there are no draw records and no runtime CLUT phases:\n  * pages: exact-static TEX with a single writer (2/1, the main member that carries the stage CLUT block); words from\n    stages-v4/stage3/textures (crc32 == TEX and sha256 == FREEZE.json re-checked);\n  * keys: listed predictions of those pages whose CLUT is a static stage-owned CLUT (owner 2/1 = stage CLUT block, or\n    2/0 = 16x1 records of the stage overlay), not all-transparent, with the highest coverage = pair_count (how often the\n    CLUT/page pair occurs in the stage model data) >= MIN_PAIRS and visible texels >= MIN_VIS of the page.  The all-zero\n    CLUT 190A55AD keys that the export labels exact-static are transparent and are not exported;\n  * cells: inferred from page content (s3cells.py, calibrated on Stage 2 draw rects, work/cells-calibration.json) and\n    rendered in isolation, the Stage 2 v2 rule; replaced by real UV rects once AQ-03 exists.\nMethod (Stage 2 method, w7-stage2 s2master copied as s3master): CLUT-free categorical index master at 8 px/texel\n(sigma 0.30 texel, power 4.0: exact native colours on plateaus, smooth contours), class forced and validated at every\nnative texel centre.  CPU only, deterministic; no generated imagery; nothing invented (no new text, colours or pixels).",
 "cells_doc": "Static cell inference for atlas pages without draw records (Stage 3 has no capture yet).\n\nStage 2 draw records showed world atlas cells are rectangles on the 32-texel grid (plus small sprites).  Without UVs, a\n32x32 block grid is joined into cells: two neighbouring blocks belong to one cell unless the 32-texel segment between\nthem is a content seam, i.e. the mean absolute index jump ACROSS the line is clearly larger than the jumps on the two\ncolumn (row) pairs next to it on either side:  across > ratio * max(within_a, within_b) and across > min_jump.\nA continuous texture (a tiling wall, one big panel) has no seam inside, so it stays one cell; a change of texture at a\ngrid line separates the cells.  Cells are connected components of blocks (any shape); render isolation uses the\ncomponent mask (texels outside the component are filled with the nearest component texel before rendering, and only\nthe component's own pixels are pasted).  This is an inference: it is replaced by real UV rects after the AQ-03 capture.",
