 "honest_read": "Inspected staging review sheets 01-07 and an 8x crop of the CAUTION plate (2026-11-13, lane-s3). Colours exact, classes exact (28 files, 0 mismatches). The CAUTION letters (E49BC3F1, lower right) keep the native glyph topology and stroke widths; corners are slightly rounded and nothing is added or removed. The grey stipple inside the strokes and on the plate turns into rounded blobs. This is the weakest part of the set: the categorical smoothing has no answer for dithered noise. The E49BC3F1 brick/stone wall (upper left) and the granite-like fill on the AA5DBEF2 prop panels become a cellular \"camouflage\" pattern at 16x, and it is still visible at the 9 px/texel in-game SIMULATION. That reads worse than the native dither for those surfaces. Vent slats (AA5DBEF2) become beaded ovals. Smoke puffs, line-art decals and solid panels look clean. The \"S. TL.\" / \"T DL...H\" plate marks keep their shapes. Partial-visibility keys (E49BC3F1 at 77-87 %, AA5DBEF2-31FCCE35 at 71 %) hide some cells under 0-entries, as the native does. Verdict: acceptable for the lettering, solid panels and decals; the dithered stone and granite surfaces should not ship from this method (they need a material rebuild or should stay native).",
